;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual, LLVM's code generator and the debugger runs; for the user's
;; review). Why this is right:
;; - The main module of a program of two: poc -emit-macro32
;;   VaxMethods.mod writes it and its import's VaxMethLib.mar
;;   (expected-vax-VaxMethLib.mar), assembled and linked together.
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 6): a record's descriptor has its
;;   ProcTab below the tag, slot i at -4(i+1), so the last slot is
;;   written first, as on LLVM (LLVMTypes.SlotMethod). SquareDesc's holds
;;   its own Area, slot 0, then CircleDesc's Hidden, hidden in VaxMethLib
;;   but overridden there, and ShapeDesc's Code; Twice's its own Add, then
;;   Counter's Get and AddAll; Local's Thrice, L_TD_1, inherits Twice's.
;;   Box has none and gets no ProcTab. Another module's procedure is its
;;   symbol, declared .EXTERNAL.
;; - A type-bound procedure is <Module>.<Type>.<P>'s symbol, after the
;;   record a pointer receiver's type points to (section 5), and always
;;   .ENTRY, global, since an importer's ProcTab may name it.
;; - Its receiver is its first argument: a pointer at 4(AP), or a VAR
;;   record's address at 4(AP) and its tag at 8(AP), as for any VAR record
;;   parameter; the other parameters follow (Twice.Add's k at 12(AP)). A
;;   receiver the procedure changes is copied to the frame (Bump's n).
;; - A call through a pointer, or a VAR record parameter or a guard on one,
;;   or p^, whose dynamic type may differ, loads the tag into R1 - the
;;   block's -4(Rn), the parameter's own (Use's c, 8(AP)) - and CALLG
;;   list, @-4(i+1)(R1). The receiver is checked for NIL first (trap 4 at
;;   the receiver). cp^.Add's tag is taken from the address in the list
;;   (SUBL3 #4 and MOVL @), cp.Add's directly, MOVL -4(R0).
;; - A record variable, field or element has its static type, so its
;;   procedure is called directly, with that type's descriptor as the tag
;;   (k.Add, box.cs[i].Add, L.total.Add); so is v.P^, the base type's
;;   procedure (Square's Area calls CircleDesc's, Twice's Add Counter's,
;;   Narrow's s.Area^ in WITH s: Square too).
;; - A call's result survives the next call in R2, saved by the entry mask
;;   (Sum, Narrow, the sum of box's counts).
;; - The run (run-values): codes 1100, 2327, 2611, dispatched 111, counted
;;   7, twice 143, sum 10, bumped 53, block 21, static 35, guarded 4214,
;;   local 183, narrowed 11148, imported 1900, total 1001, all 21, last 9;
;;   q's tag SquareDesc's descriptor (its size 6 shown), its ProcTab
;;   Square's Area (mask ^M<R2>, 4), CircleDesc's Hidden (0) and
;;   ShapeDesc's Code (4). Modes 1 to 3 trap 4, 5 and 4 at 85:35, 51:9 and
;;   87:34, where the LLVM backend's -trap-location puts them (run-*-trap).
; VaxMethods, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
